# --------------------- utl tvg options ---------------------
# flopy multi-package
# flopy subpackage tvg6_filerecord tvg tvg_array tvg_array
# flopy parent_name_type parent_package MFPackage

block options
name readarraygrid
type keyword
shape
reader urword
optional false
longname use grid-array input
description indicates that grid-array input will be used for the TVG Utility.  This keyword must be specified to use grid-array input.
default_value true

block options
name auxiliary
type string
shape (naux)
reader urword
optional true
longname keyword to specify aux variables
description REPLACE auxnames {'{#1}': 'Time-Varying Grid arrays'}

block options
name print_input
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname print input to listing file
description REPLACE print_input {'{#1}': 'time-varying grid array input'}
mf6internal iprpak

block options
name export_array_netcdf
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
mf6internal export_nc
longname export array variables to netcdf output files.
description keyword that specifies input griddata arrays should be written to the model output netcdf file.
extended true

block options
name tas_filerecord
type record tas6 filein tas6_filename
shape
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description

block options
name tas6
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname time-array series keyword
description keyword to specify that record corresponds to a time-array-series file.

block options
name filein
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname file keyword
description keyword to specify that an input filename is expected next.

block options
name tas6_filename
type string
preserve_case true
in_record true
reader urword
optional false
tagged false
longname file name of time series information
description defines a time-array-series file defining a time-array series that can be used to assign time-varying values. See the ``Time-Variable Input'' section for instructions on using the time-array series capability.

# --------------------- utl tvg period ---------------------

block period
name iper
type integer
block_variable true
in_record true
tagged false
shape
valid
reader urword
optional false
longname stress period number
description REPLACE iper {}

block period
name aux
type double precision
shape (nodes)
reader readarray
time_series true
layered true
netcdf true
optional true
longname auxiliary variable iaux
description is an array of values for auxiliary variable aux(iaux), where iaux is a value from 1 to naux, and aux(iaux) must be listed as part of the auxiliary variables.  A separate array can be specified for each auxiliary variable.  A value other than DNODATA (3.0E+30) at an active cell replaces the current value for that cell; an array not specified in a PERIOD block keeps its values.  An array can be defined by a time-array series (see the ``Using Time-Array Series in a Package'' section).
mf6internal auxvar
